   - As the maintainer decided on 2 October 2026, transforming a value and collecting it for the search are separate, and release is conditional on both. The release gate enforces exactly this:
     - **Coverage.** The walker reports the paths of the values it planned to collect, those it collected, those it could not collect, with a reason that holds no value, and those it read only as bytes. Collection is complete only when every planned value was collected from its decoded form under a VR that the pinned dictionary gives its attribute. It is incomplete where a planned value was neither collected nor reported as not collected, so an empty collection is never taken as complete; where a value could not be collected; where text outside ISO 646 with no Specific Character Set was read only as ISO 8859-1 (Architecture item 5), since searching its bytes supplements the coverage but does not stand in for the decoded text, whose copies in other attributes or encodings were not searched for; and where a value was collected under another VR, such as a person name collected as CS, which the search would leave out or search in the wrong forms. Coverage is pooled across the subject, as the values searched for are, so a sibling instance's gap counts against every file of the subject, even where another instance collected a value at the same path. An instance out of scope whose IOD the pinned tables define, such as a nuclear medicine image or an ultrasound image, is read, planned, and edited only so that its values are collected for its subject's search, and is never written, so that it withholds its subject's files only where its collection is incomplete, as any instance's would. Under Clean Descriptors, such an instance, like any other withheld before its descriptors are cleaned, leaves out of that collection the descriptors that cleaning would write with a kept value (D-009). This is "Collect first", which builds on "Withhold", as the maintainer decided on 6 October 2026. An instance of the subject whose values were not collected at all, because its source was refused, its SOP Class names no IOD of the pinned tables, its Specific Character Set cannot be decoded, its transform failed, or it changed during the run, withholds every file of the subject, since its values could be in them unsearched for; and where the walker sequesters an instance, the planned values it did not reach are not collected, rather than not reported. Values in an instance whose file could not be read as DICOM, which names no subject, are not pooled. File Meta Information and preamble values are not collected; the writer rewrites both, so neither is released, but a copy of one in kept text is not searched for.
     - **Search.** The gate runs the search itself, for exactly the pooled collected values, so no other search can stand in for it. The forms that the search leaves out by the rules below, such as those shorter than four characters and binary values, are its exclusions: they are listed with their reasons and never count as incomplete.
